    "ratioDecidendi": "Former directors who authorised payments of company funds after their removal, to related parties and to the first defendant himself, without board approval and not to discharge the company's own debts, breached their fiduciary duties. The judge rejected the alleged verbal agreement and held that directors may not subordinate the company's interests to those of its wider group, and that de facto directorship is assessed objectively. The first defendant's counterclaim failed because he did not work during his notice period, so he had no entitlement to salary for that period.",
