    "issues": "(1) Whether Mr Basil proved justification, fair comment and qualified privilege; (2) whether malice defeated qualified privilege and justification; (3) Mr Basil's counterclaim for wrongful dismissal and for defamation arising from Premier's letter to the Ministry of Manpower; (4) the aggravated damages to be awarded; (5) whether costs should be awarded on the High Court scale although damages were below S$250,000.",
    "ratioDecidendi": "All three defences failed: Mr Basil could not prove the truth of the defamatory imputations, the statements were not fair comment on true facts, and letters sent to parties with no shared interest were not privileged. Independently, the court found the letters were actuated by malice, a desire to avenge his dismissal, which also defeats qualified privilege and justification, so the plaintiffs recovered aggravated damages.",
