    "facts": "Cousins, a Chief Trader later demoted to Senior Trader at RBS Singapore, asked to be made redundant. On 11 May 2009 he signed a Redundancy Agreement offering S$455,085.39. Minutes later he forwarded two confidential emails to his personal Gmail account. The bank discovered this, had him delete the emails, summarily dismissed him on 22 May 2009 and rescinded the agreement. He sued for the S$455,085.39, and the bank counterclaimed S$218,599 paid earlier as a stock buyout.",
    "issues": "(a) Whether an employee already made redundant under a redundancy agreement could be summarily dismissed; (b) whether the breach of the confidentiality obligation was a repudiatory breach of the Redundancy Agreement entitling the bank to terminate it (the RDC Concrete situations); (c) whether the bank could recover the January 2009 stock buyout under the employment contract.",
